WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.400
Here's what done looks like.

2
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:06.413
The register runs every week, and every
ownerless row has a ticket with an owner.

3
00:00:06.413 --> 00:00:11.487
Every exposure that went away had
its DNS records checked and removed.

4
00:00:11.487 --> 00:00:14.329
Defender for Cloud's
export was reconciled,

5
00:00:14.329 --> 00:00:18.038
and every gap is either added
to the queries or explained.

6
00:00:18.038 --> 00:00:21.801
And the register and its run
folders live inside the boundary.

7
00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:27.720
Next, Chapter 3 traces each public IP in
this register to its DDoS protection.
